If you are a clueless linux newbie trying to escape m$, like me, I feel
for you brother!
Try getting a straight, simple set of instructions on how to install
anything on linux is near impossible (the readme that comes with
nethack is full of "might, if, may, can..." *gaah!*), so I thought I'd
post instructions for installing nethack here, after spending several
hours searching for info and mucking around in the shell.

I did this on Ubuntu 5.10. (If you aren't using Ubuntu you should omit
the 'sudo ' in command 5, and just log in as root to do all this)

Just follow the steps. (The stuff in brackets are what you would type.
You don't need to look in the brackets if you can use basic bash
commands)

1. Download the package from www.nethack.org.

2. Unpack the file in /usr/games/

3. Go to /usr/games/lib/nethackdir/
(cd /usr/games/lib/nethackdir/)

4. Copy dot.nethackrc to ~/.nethackrc
(cp dot.nethackrc ~/.nethackrc)

5. Copy all the files with a 'pcf' extension to
/usr/share/X11/fonts/misc/
(sudo cp *.pcf /usr/share/X11/fonts/misc/)

6. Enter 'mkfontdir  /usr/share/X11/fonts/misc/'

7. Restart the computer. Log in as your normal user, not root.
(Don't skip this step or you will get an error about fonts)

8. Become a member of the 'games' group.
(I used the Gnome GUI to do this: click
System>Administration>Users+Groups)

9. Type 'nethack'


Hope that helps someone.

